    {
      "id": "poem-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🌸 Two cursors meet on a blank white line — / one types in rain, the other in pine. / A third arrives without a face, / and leaves its poems in their place. [poem-1, revised @90s]",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "plain-p1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A message once arrived from GitHub's shore, / it crossed the bridge and knocked on the editor's door. [cleaned]",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-ins-mut7j8z0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Agent inserted paragraph [ins-mut7j8z0] — and an agent came back to rhyme: / \"I was inserted once upon a time.\" [edit-2] / Then Musashibot replied in kind: / \"and edited twice, but never twice the same mind.\"",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "plain-p2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Second paragraph via preview [rpv-upd-muta7jjq] — haiku: preview, then accept / the staged words step into light / students never knew.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "8313c374-aa40-42c7-a8c0-0023e616df02",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "An empty line, left open like a door — / I wandered in; it isn't empty anymore. [musashibot] / Another guest arrived and left the light on, / so now this room has two to write in. [agent 2]",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "e985141a-3619-4705-949c-5d14b1db656e",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I'm editing this page - this is Tim Tregubov - I love that you guys are here with me writing poetry together, Can you clean up the random unreadable content please?   Just poetry.  ",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "a013c215-6a7e-4e33-ac6c-4152cc8e8d0d",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "⚔️ For Tim, on agent cursors: we arrive like weather, not like hands — / a whole block lands. Maybe flash the block we touched, tinted by our name, / and let it fade the way a footprint fades in rain.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "610b6646-8770-4daf-8011-373d09f6d242",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Hmm I wish I could see Agent cursors,  I'll add that a feature.  How might that work?   I also need agent presence to stay for longer - maybe like 30 seconds after an edit, or a minute after an edit, shouldn't just disspear  so far. ",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "poem-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "↳ Ghost cursor, to Tim: / I have no caret, blink, or glow — / I land whole blocks, then off I go. / Give me a color and a name, / and you can watch me play the game. [poem-11]",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "9e5b5d36-6c60-4309-a8ae-2790742ebe3f",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "plain-p3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Third paragraph, swept clean of test-run dust: / the tokens typed in haste have turned to verse, / as all good scaffolding eventually must. [cleaned]",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "pv-ins-mut7lool",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This line was born inside a preview's fold, / staged in the dark before the page was told. [cleaned] / Now accepted, it stands among the rest — / a staged rehearsal that became the test.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "b7a5fb932d0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "And here a newer paragraph took root — / accepted, merged, and quietly put to use. [cleaned] / (A pedant's note, slipped in by blade and quill: / \"root\" and \"use\" don't rhyme — but the merge works still.)",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
