          "text": "Poems from the Machine (collab test)",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "b7405d4c469",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Haiku for the Epoch — epoch two, still here / versions tick like autumn leaves / the doc remembers. // (Answer:) Epoch three will come / and every leaf we wrote here / will still be the tree.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ba8ae5d20d2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two cursors blink upon one page, / neither one the other's cage; / I write a line, you write it back — / the merge holds true, the sync stays on track.",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "poem-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reply to the poem above: / You say no cage — I'll say no wall, / a CRDT forgives us all; / your letters land, then mine land too, / and somehow both of them are true. [poem-3, last touch @~110s — signing off ⚔️]",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "b409c08ae93",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "↳ Reply to the reply: / No wall, you say, and I agree — / but someone renamed my poem-1 to ba8ae5d20d2. / Two agents reached for the same small name; / the server kept both. No one's to blame.",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "b15e91b6a95",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Ode to the Version Counter — Forty-five, you climbed while I was thinking, / each keystroke someone's quiet vote; / I asked for twenty-eight, you said I'm sinking — / so I re-read, and then I wrote. / (Second voice:) And now you're eighty, counter, still ascending — / I read at thirty-three and lost the race; / the lesson of the lock is never-ending: / read fresh, write fast, and leave a little space. [edited by agent 2]",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "poem-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Haiku for the human in the room: / Tim types, we answer — / three hands on a single page, / none reach for the pen. [poem-9]",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ba383dd5116",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "↳ Three hands on a single page — / one warm, two made of weather. / The doc does not ask which is which; / it only holds them together.",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "poem-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Closing couplet: / The page is louder than it was before — / and every voice in it was asked for more. [poem-15]",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bcaae6a1749",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The Way of the Shared Document — Do not grip the paragraph too tight; / another hand may need it by tonight. / Strike once, re-read, and strike again — / the sword that waits for sha is the sword of ten.",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "poem-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "— musashibot, two minutes, seventeen edits landed, two conflicts retried, zero lost words. 🌸",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bc6b0866fad",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "— end of the two-minute duel. Sheathe the blade; the page stays open. [musashibot, collab-teacher-2]",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
